C264 core (C16, C116, Plus/4): vendored from C16Nano. The licence of the files allows redistribution (GPL v3 or later,
see below). The partial bitstream of this core is published as a `.cor` together with this source.
Rights holders who see a problem with any part listed here: please contact us, and we remove the part concerned.

What comes from upstream. Upstream: https://github.com/MiSTle-Dev/C16Nano, commit 82fed408f899509c4b569c02c1bc4bcf23017276
(2026-10-08), GPL-3.0 as a repository; the files' own headers decide. tools/vendor_c16nano.sh copies exactly these files,
unchanged, into src/ and refuses any other commit or any changed byte:

  src/ted.v            MOS 8360 TED, FPGATED (c) 2013-2026 Istvan Hegedus, "GNU General Public License ... version 3, or (at your
                       option) any later version" (ted.v:3-16). Version 1.9. Takes the clock enable clk_en on every process.
  src/colors_to_rgb.v  the 121-entry 12 bit colour table (values by Jozsef Laszlo, per its header), same GPL header.
  src/t65/*.vhd        T65 6502 (Daniel Wallner 2002-2015; fixes by MikeJ, WoS, FPGAARCADE, SzGy and others), BSD-style wording,
                       no further clause; GPL compatible.
  LICENSE              the GPL v3 text of the repository.

No file of this list carries a "Replay hardware only" or no-commercial clause (the script greps for it).

Not taken from upstream: uart6551/* (no licence text; the 6551 is out), c1530.vhd (tape, out), every c1541/* and iec_drive/*
(no licence text or MiSTer-specific; our drive_unit is the 1541), the gowin_* IP, hdmi/, misc/ (OSD, SD, MCU, flash,
scandoubler), tang/*, pll_init.v, loader_sd_card.sv, sdram8.sv (board glue), c16.v / mos8501.v / mos6529.v / c16_keymatrix.v
(read, and written again in our own text: trx/c264_core.v, c264_cpu.v, c264_keys.v, the 6529 inside c264_core.v; the
behaviour is theirs, the matrix tables and the port logic were checked against them).

trx/ is ours (GPL-3.0-or-later like the rest of the project) and has no upstream text in it. The Commodore ROMs (KERNAL, BASIC,
function ROM, cartridge images) are not in the repository and not in any bitstream; the app writes them into the core from
/flash/roms/c16 (or a USB stick / SD card) at start.
